      "worked": "The domain is $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$, since $1+2^{1/x}>0$ whenever $x\\ne0$. This domain is symmetric about zero.\n\nFor every $x\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{1-2^{-1/x}}{1+2^{-1/x}}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{1-\\frac{1}{2^{1/x}}}{1+\\frac{1}{2^{1/x}}}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{2^{1/x}-1}{2^{1/x}+1}\\\\f(-x)&=-\\frac{1-2^{1/x}}{1+2^{1/x}}\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $f$ is odd.",
